      "content": "<h3>9. comparator(), clone, equals and toString</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Signature:</strong> <code>Comparator<? super K> comparator();  Object clone();  boolean equals(Object);  String toString()</code></li>\n<li><strong>Returns:</strong> the ordering / a shallow copy / comparison / text</li>\n<li><strong>Time:</strong> O(n)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>For freshers:</strong> <code>comparator()</code> returns the ordering in use (<code>null</code> for natural ordering). A TreeMap is <code>equal</code> to any Map with the same pairs, whatever the order or class.</p>\n<p><strong>For experienced developers:</strong> A <code>clone</code> copies the structure and keeps the comparator. Because <code>equals</code> on maps uses <code>equals</code> of the keys, a TreeMap with an unusual comparator can be \"not equal\" to a HashMap that looks identical.</p>",
      "codeExamples": [
        "// TreeMap comparator() / clone / equals\nimport java.util.Comparator;\nimport java.util.HashMap;\nimport java.util.Map;\nimport java.util.TreeMap;\n\npublic class TreeMapComparatorDemo {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        TreeMap<String, Integer> natural = new TreeMap<>(Map.of(\"Raigad\", 6, \"Torna\", 5));\n        TreeMap<String, Integer> reverse = new TreeMap<>(Comparator.reverseOrder());\n        reverse.putAll(natural);\n\n        System.out.println(\"natural.comparator() : \" + natural.comparator());\n        System.out.println(\"reverse.comparator() is set: \" + (reverse.comparator() != null));\n        System.out.println(\"natural : \" + natural + \"   reverse : \" + reverse);\n        System.out.println(\"equal?  : \" + natural.equals(reverse));            // same pairs, so equal\n\n        Map<String, Integer> hash = new HashMap<>(natural);\n        System.out.println(\"equals a HashMap with the same pairs: \" + natural.equals(hash));\n\n        @SuppressWarnings(\"unchecked\")\n        TreeMap<String, Integer> copy = (TreeMap<String, Integer>) reverse.clone();\n        copy.put(\"Lohagad\", 2);\n        System.out.println(\"clone keeps the comparator: \" + copy);\n    }\n}\n// OUTPUT:\n// natural.comparator() : null\n// reverse.comparator() is set: true\n// natural : {Raigad=6, Torna=5}   reverse : {Torna=5, Raigad=6}\n// equal?  : true\n// equals a HashMap with the same pairs: true\n// clone keeps the comparator: {Torna=5, Raigad=6, Lohagad=2}"
      ]
