      "content": "<h3>Real example 1: tax / price slabs with floorEntry</h3>\n<p>A table of slabs keyed by the <strong>lower bound</strong>. <code>floorEntry(amount)</code> finds the slab that contains any amount in one O(log n) call.</p>",
      "codeExamples": [
        "// Entry fee slabs: the slab that contains a group size\nimport java.util.Map;\nimport java.util.TreeMap;\n\npublic class TreeMapSlabsDemo {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        TreeMap<Integer, Integer> feePerPerson = new TreeMap<>();   // key = smallest group size of the slab\n        feePerPerson.put(1, 100);       // 1 to 9 people pay 100 each\n        feePerPerson.put(10, 80);       // 10 to 24 people pay 80 each\n        feePerPerson.put(25, 60);       // 25 or more pay 60 each\n\n        for (int group : new int[] {1, 9, 10, 24, 25, 100}) {\n            Map.Entry<Integer, Integer> slab = feePerPerson.floorEntry(group);\n            System.out.println(\"Group of \" + group + \" -> slab starting at \" + slab.getKey() + \", fee \" + slab.getValue() + \" each, total \" + group * slab.getValue());\n        }\n    }\n}\n// OUTPUT:\n// Group of 1 -> slab starting at 1, fee 100 each, total 100\n// Group of 9 -> slab starting at 1, fee 100 each, total 900\n// Group of 10 -> slab starting at 10, fee 80 each, total 800\n// Group of 24 -> slab starting at 10, fee 80 each, total 1920\n// Group of 25 -> slab starting at 25, fee 60 each, total 1500\n// Group of 100 -> slab starting at 25, fee 60 each, total 6000"
      ]
